Fill in the Extruder Start/End G-code too, and split the prime line

The machine Start and End G-code were already set, but Cura has FOUR G-code
fields spread over two tabs of Machine settings, and the two on the Extruder tab
were still empty:

  Printer tab  -> machine_start_gcode / machine_end_gcode       (were set)
  Extruder tab -> machine_extruder_start_code / _end_code       (empty)

Those two live in fdmextruder.def.json with default_value = "" and belong to the
EXTRUDER container, not the machine one, so they need their own template,
cura_profile/extruder_definition_changes.inst.cfg, written to
definition_changes/voron2_extruder_0+%232_settings.inst.cfg.

The prime line moves out of the machine start G-code into the extruder start
code, which is where Cura expects it, and the retract moves into the extruder
end code, so nothing runs twice. The order is still: machine start, extruder
start, print, extruder end, machine end. The extruder end block wraps its
retract in G91/G90 because Cura leaves the printer in absolute E, and a bare
G1 E-2 would mean "E = -2".

install-cura-profile.ps1 now applies both templates in one pass, keyed off the
"definition = ..." line of each container, and refuses to run while Cura is open
(exit 2) instead of prompting, so a write cannot be silently lost when Cura
rewrites these files on exit.

Applied on the machine with Cura closed, and verified by replaying Cura's own
FastConfigParser regex over both files.
